# ---- sub-exclude: paths withheld even though their verdict is scrub ----
# An entry is either a whole path or a single file inside a scrub directory.
# A file is withheld when it equals an entry or lives under one. This lets the
# foundations DOCTRINE ship (scrubbed) while the biography beside it stays home
# (Keaton's word 20260808 -- share the doctrine, withhold only the bio).
# `context` is NOT here -- its gitignored personal overrides (a real PUBKEYS.md,
# a filled GLOW_*.bron) are already untracked, so git ls-files never offers them.

# whole-path:
# ---- gratitude: two classes withheld, and each for a different law ----------------------
#
# COPYRIGHT, not privacy. A saved third-party article is somebody else's writing held for study
# (gratitude-licenses.md: a reading library, never a dependency). Shipping the field's own copy to
# a public repository would republish it, which is a different act from thanking its author.
sub_exclude gratitude/Your customers hate MVPs. Make a SLC instead..html
#
# LICENCE, not privacy. Every project below is held as a GITLINK precisely so our history never
# contains its source (gratitude-licenses.md, the GPL-3.0 and LGPL-2.1 tables). tools/s/sow.rish
# copies files and knows nothing of gitlinks, so today it ships empty directories -- these are
# unchecked-out on this pier, measured 20260906. That safety is INCIDENTAL, and a hand who checks
# one out for a read would turn it structural-into-a-leak. Named by path so it cannot.
sub_exclude gratitude/ai-jail
sub_exclude gratitude/damus
sub_exclude gratitude/dawk
sub_exclude gratitude/dvui
sub_exclude gratitude/grain-sketchbook
sub_exclude gratitude/infuse.nix
sub_exclude gratitude/libqrencode
sub_exclude gratitude/manyana
sub_exclude gratitude/nips
